index 4479b53..4a53069 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -9,6 +9,39 @@ pnpm install && pnpm run start
 
 The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 
+## WebMCP
+
+On browsers that provide WebMCP, the shared layout registers tools using
+`document.modelContext`, with a fallback to the older `navigator.modelContext`.
+Browsers without either API continue to work normally; no polyfill or external
+MCP server is required. The implementation follows the
+[WebMCP draft](https://webmachinelearning.github.io/webmcp/).
+
+| Tool | Input | Result |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `search_articles` | `query`, optional `limit` (1–50, default 10) | Matching article slugs, titles, summaries, links, and total count |
+| `get_reading_list` | `{}` | Saved articles for the current session |
+| `save_article` | `slug` from search results | Saved state and reading-list slugs |
+| `remove_saved_article` | `slug` | Saved state and reading-list slugs |
+
+Search uses the same title/summary matching logic as the search flyout. Reading
+list mutations reuse the session API and notify the React UI. Explicit save and
+remove actions are idempotent. The API's existing `{ slug }` POST still toggles
+bookmarks; `{ slug, saved: true/false }` sets the desired state.
+
+Tools register once per document and stay available across Astro client-side
+navigation. Failed registration is rolled back and retried on a later page load.
+Tool callbacks validate inputs, propagate request failures, and forward execution
+cancellation signals to fetch. Agent access depends on browser WebMCP support
+and its permissions; this application does not expose tools over a network port.
+
+Run automated tool checks with Node 24 or newer:
+
+```sh
+node --test tests/webmcp.test.mjs
+pnpm run build
+```
+
 ## Tech Stack
 
 - **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
